tated. Overall, the mathematical notation is clear and consistent, and the derivations are well-explained.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-023","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The figures and tables are effectively used to support the narrative. Figure 1 clearly illustrates the different architectures for the integration of latent variables in a feedforward neural network (FNN), with the concatenation and bilinear integration clearly labeled. Figure 2 provides a clear overview of the hierarchical SNN architecture used to solve downstream tasks. Figure 3 shows the different mazes used in the experiments, with clear labels for each maze. Figure 4 presents the span of skills learned by different methods and architectures, with clear labels for each method and architecture. Figure 5 shows the visitation plots for different randomly initialized architectures, with clear labels for each architecture. Figure 6 presents the faster learning of the hierarchical architectures in the sparse downstream MDPs, with clear labels for each task. The captions are detailed and provide sufficient context for the reader to understand the figures. The tables are readable and provide clear information. Overall, the figures and tables are well-designed and effectively support the narrative.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"869792ca6e5fea579caba576410dc8fff7590493e6de7144f0555bdc7e4a7ae9","paper_id":"B1oK8aoxe","paper_ordinal":15,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"91f8dca9c75ef1c925c9ba6ebe28d758e90619b4863e2226071937bd9aec1392","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1oK8aoxe","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"c60c200991aa36a392611ffe594b7b2e428934b65bad3e31941030d63576412c","requ